    rdau:P61101 "<a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Gruyter'>Wikipedia</a>, katsottu 29.7.2025 (Several former publishing houses have become imprints of De Gruyter: \"De Gruyter Mouton/De Gruyter Saur\" (formerly \"Mouton de Gruyter\") was purchased by de Gruyter in 1977. It was originally known as Mouton Publishers and based in The Hague. The imprint specializes in the field of linguistics and publishes academic journals, research monographs, reference works, multimedia publications, and bibliographies.)"@fi,
        "<a href='https://www.degruyterbrill.com/publishing/about-us/about-de-gruyter-brill/our-brands/de-gruyter-mouton'>Yhteisön verkkosivut</a>, katsottu 29.7.2025 (In 1977, De Gruyter acquired the publishing company Mouton Publishers, which Pierre-François Mouton founded in Paris in 1858. ... The merger with De Gruyter created De Gruyter Mouton as a dedicated imprint for publishing linguistic and cultural studies works.)"@fi,
        "The forms of meaning, 2000 nimiösivu (Mouton de Gruyter, Berlin, New York), kolofoni (Mouton de Gruyter (formerly Mouton, The Hague) is a Division of Walter de Gruyter & Co. KG, Berlin)"@fi ;
